# Test fixtures are extractor *inputs*, not build output.
#
# rust-port was folded into DevCouncil from a standalone repository, which
# moved the git worktree root up one level. `extract` walks with
# `WalkBuilder.git_ignore(true)` and reads ignore rules from that root, so the
# parent's Python-packaging patterns (`lib/`, `build/`, `var/`, `dist/`,
# `share/`) began governing which fixture files get indexed:
# `testdata/vendor/lib/x.py` silently stopped being walked and the testdata
# determinism digest moved. Language fixtures legitimately use those directory
# names, so re-include the whole tree here — a nested ignore file takes
# precedence over the parent's, and the directory must be re-included before
# any file inside it can be.
!testdata/
!testdata/**
# …but never the generated stores or OS cruft that live inside fixtures.
testdata/**/.devcouncil/
testdata/**/.DS_Store
